# AIOS engine — repository ignore rules.
#
# The engine's source, its measurement results and the Kaggle kernel bundles are
# all committed. Model weights are NOT: they are large (0.5 GB - 6.2 GB), are
# reproducible from the HF repo with training/native/c1/fetch_05b.py +
# export_small.py, and exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit anyway.

# ---- model weights and caches (reproducible, too large for git) ----
training/native/c1/model/weights.bin
training/native/c1/model_05b/
training/native/c1/model3b_meta/weights.bin
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin

# ---- build outputs (regenerated by the check harnesses) ----
training/native/b4/out/
training/native/b4/tmp/
training/native/b1/b1_exit42.elf
training/native/b1/b1_exit42.elf.code.bin
**/*.elf
**/*.o

# ---- Python bytecode ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- scratch / local-only ----
.freebuff/
scratch/
*.log
.cred_in
.cred_in2

# ---- built corpus (from the 135M instruct fine-tune pipeline) ----
# Project internals: stays local / on Kaggle.
data/train.txt
data/val.txt
*.zip

# NOTE: .freebuff/project-id is a local Freebuff Desktop pointer and is
# explicitly not to be committed (see .freebuff/.gitignore in the tree).
